  51:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c **** /**
  52:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   * @brief It submits the request for moving the state machine into the state
  53:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        specified by bState (FAULT_NOW and FAUL_OVER are not handled by this
  54:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        method). Accordingly with the current state, the command is really
  55:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        executed (state machine set to bState) or discarded (no state
  56:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        changes).
  57:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        If requested state can't be reached the return value is false and the
  58:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        MC_SW_ERROR is raised, but if requested state is IDLE_START,
  59:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        IDLE_ALIGNMENT or ANY_STOP, that corresponds with the user actions:
  60:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        Start Motor, Encoder Alignemnt and Stop Motor, the MC_SW_ERROR is
  61:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *        not raised.
  62:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   * @param pHanlde pointer of type  STM_Handle_t.
  63:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   * @param bState New requested state
  64:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   * @retval bool It returns true if the state has been really set equal to
  65:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   *         bState, false if the requested state can't be reached
  66:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/state_machine.c ****   */
